*** Add File:demo/README_DEMO.md
+# Aegis LLM Adapter Demo — Build, Deploy, Run Pilot
+
+Prereqs:
+- Docker and kubectl configured to a cluster (kind/minikube/GKE/EKS).  
+- A local Docker registry running at localhost:5000 (or edit demo/run_demo.sh to push to your registry).  
+- Secrets: create k8s secret `llm-secrets` in namespace `ml` with keys `openai_api_key` and `anthropic_api_key` if you plan to call vendors.
+
+Quick run:
+1. Start local registry if needed (e.g., `docker run -d -p 5000:5000 --restart=always --name registry registry:2`)  
+2. Build & deploy & run pilot:
+   ./demo/run_demo.sh
+3. Check results:
+   /tmp/aegis_llm_pilot/results.csv
+
+Notes on private endpoints / VPC:
+- For production or VPC-restricted access, configure provider SDKs and client libraries to use private endpoints:
+  - OpenAI: set OPENAI_API_BASE to your proxy/private endpoint.
+  - Anthropic: set ANTHROPIC_API_BASE / use Anthropic Private Network if offered.
+  - Google: set AIP_API_ENDPOINT env var and ensure Workload Identity / private service connect is configured.
+- Update k8s annotations in k8s/llm-adapter-deployment.yaml to match your cloud provider's private endpoint annotations.
+
